        "original_id": "7e44ed30-885b-5126-b592-3ef4e33f8d80",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: Mmm Papi, La Isla Bonita, Whiplash, Rock Me In\n- People: Madonna, Patrick Leonard, Bruce Gaitsch, Selena Gomez, Destinee & Paris, Britney Spears, Michael Jackson, Christina Aguilera, Beyoncé, Katy Perry, Rihanna, Gwen Stefani\n- Albums: True Blue\n- Places: New Jersey, Los Angeles\n- Concepts: Latin pop influence\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, Madonna released \"La Isla Bonita\" on her third studio album \"True Blue\".\n- In 1987, Madonna's song \"La Isla Bonita\" was noted as a Latin pop song.\n- Madonna and Patrick Leonard co-wrote and co-produced \"La Isla Bonita\", and Bruce Gaitsch contributed additional songwriting.\n- \"Mmm Papi\" is noted for having a Latin pop influence similar to Madonna's \"La Isla Bonita\".\n- The writers mentioned together wrote the songs \"Mmm Papi\", \"Rock Me In\", and \"Whiplash\".\n- Destinee & Paris were born and raised in New Jersey and later became based in Los Angeles.\n- Destinee & Paris cited Britney Spears, Michael Jackson, Christina Aguilera, Beyoncé, Katy Perry, Rihanna, and Gwen Stefani as influences.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
